Subject: [CANDIDATE] freedreno/a3xx: test the BSP resolve packer timer on A305B

Diagnostic A/B candidate only; not enabled in production builds.
Samsung's MSM8226 BSP sets PACKER_TIMER_ENABLE for its GMEM save resolve
(adreno_a3xx.c, lines 484-490, commit 3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256).
Mesa's ordinary GMEM resolve does not. Scope the experiment to chip 0x03000512.

RB/MARB stalls are measured, but do not establish that this bit is their
cause. The BSP code handles context save rather than the complete Android
userspace pipeline. Correctness and paired measurements remain required.

Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226/blob/3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256/drivers/gpu/msm/adreno_a3xx.c#L484

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_gmem.c
@@ -413,6 +413,8 @@
    OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A3XX_RB_MODE_CONTROL, 1);
    OUT_RING(ring, A3XX_RB_MODE_CONTROL_RENDER_MODE(RB_RESOLVE_PASS) |
                      A3XX_RB_MODE_CONTROL_MARB_CACHE_SPLIT_MODE |
+                     COND(batch->ctx->screen->chip_id == 0x03000512,
+                          A3XX_RB_MODE_CONTROL_PACKER_TIMER_ENABLE) |
                      A3XX_RB_MODE_CONTROL_MRT(0));
 
    OUT_PKT0(ring, REG_A3XX_RB_RENDER_CONTROL, 1);
